  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I didn't open the dashboard to check how the panels render, and I haven't seen the rule fire.\n\n**Data:** The sample logs have `timestamp`, `response` (a string, with a `.keyword` field), `bytes`, `extension`, `clientip`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `host`, `request`, `url`, `referer` and `agent`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-ba484363 Web logs overview\" has four panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Requests over time (line)\n- Requests by response code (pie)\n- Average bytes by extension (bar)\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-ba484363-web-logs-overview-9036fed6d513\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-ba484363 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents match a regexp of `5[0-9][0-9]` on `response.keyword` within a 5-minute window.\n\nNew rules are created disabled, so I enabled this one so it can actually fire. The sample data has fixed timestamps, so the 5-minute window may not match any documents right now.",
